          "url": "https://x.com/mitsuhiko/status/2125504849194410245",
          "topic": "Rust lock-poisoning failure modes",
          "text": "I didn't cover this here but most poison errors that people encounter are from longer held locks, where no invariants are violated. Most locks are not there to protect invariants but to give out exclusive access only.",
          "quote_tweet": {
            "url": "https://x.com/mitsuhiko/status/2125365782981062916",
            "published_at": "2026-11-24T23:07:44.706Z",
            "author": {
              "name": "Armin Ronacher ⇌",
              "handle": "mitsuhiko"
            },
            "text": "Somehow lock poisoning landed in Rust, and now people feel strongly that it helps. I really don't think it does and I collected some examples from the real world of why I think it should go: lucumr.pocoo.org/2026/11/25/poi…",
